### 1、pingpong(easy)

#### Question requirements

> Write a program that uses UNIX system calls to ''ping-pong'' a byte between two processes over a pair of pipes, one for each direction. The parent should send a byte to the child; the child should print "<pid>: received ping", where <pid> is its process ID, write the byte on the pipe to the parent, and exit; the parent should read the byte from the child, print "<pid>: received pong", and exit. Your solution should be in the file user/pingpong.c.

#### Some hints

> - Use pipe to create a pipe.
> - Use fork to create a child.
> - Use read to read from the pipe, and write to write to the pipe.
> - Use getpid to find the process ID of the calling process.
> - Add the program to UPROGS in Makefile.
> - User programs on xv6 have a limited set of library functions available to them. You can see - the list in user/user.h;
> - the source  (other than for system calls) is in user/ulib.c, user/printf.c, and
> - user/umalloc.c.

#### Run the program from the xv6 shell and it should produce the following output

```bash
 $ make qemu
 ...
 init: starting sh
 $ pingpong
 4: received ping
 3: received pong
 $
```
#### Solution

```c
#include "kernel/types.h"
#include "kernel/stat.h"
#include "user/user.h"

int main() {
    char buf[10] = {0};
    // 将用不到的文件描述符尽可能全部关闭
    int p1[2], p2[2];
    pipe(p1); // 父进程发
    pipe(p2); // 子进程发

    int pid = fork();
    if (pid == 0) {
        const char *message = "S";
        // 子进程:在 p2 中发送,p1 中接收
        close(0);
        close(2);

        close(p1[1]);
        close(p2[0]);

        // 接收
        read(p1[0], buf, 10);
        fprintf(1,"%d: received ping\n", getpid());
        close(p1[0]);
        // 发送

        write(p2[1], message, 2);
        // 发送完就关闭
        close(p2[1]);
        exit(0);
    } else if (pid > 0) {
        const char *message = "F";
        // 父进程:在 p1 中 发送,p2 中 接收
        close(0);
        close(2);

        close(p1[0]);
        close(p2[1]);

        // 发送
        write(p1[1], message, 2);
        // 发送完就关闭
        close(p1[1]);
        // 接收
        read(p2[0], buf, 10);
        close(p2[0]);

        int status;
        wait(&status);// 防止抢占1
        fprintf(1,"%d: received pong\n", getpid());

    } else {
        fprintf(1,"err for fork()\n");
        exit(1);
    }
    exit(0);
}
```

